text:
ralph: Heads-up: i'm opening a docs PR to clarify model-catalog limits and add small migration examples for polaris13b and ardent3b. Need audit of keys, a CLI alias note, and a short benchmark footnote. PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/4782
mina: Nice. Which keys are changing? We standardized on `max_sequence_length` last quarter. Also avoid the old `sequence_limit` key in examples.
ralph: Exactly. Replace `sequence_limit` -> `max_sequence_length` everywhere. Also include a one-line paragraph: 'Variant ceilings are hardware-dependent; see catalog CSV for per-variant values.'
cheng: Runtime provided ceilings: polaris13b(fp16)=8192, polaris13b-quant=6144, ardent3b(fp16)=6144, ardent3b-quant=4096. They asked we prefix with "variant-dependent" and link to /data/model-catalog.csv.
sasha: i'll add two compact snippets: 1) SDK v4 resolveVariant + generate with try/catch fallback to compat alias, 2) CLI curl example showing alias `polaris13b:compat-q4_0`. Keep both under 8 lines.
runtime-bot: Note from runtime: kernel selection may change effective ceiling by +/- 512 tokens on some GPU families. Recommend wording: "ceiling may vary slightly by GPU family and kernel selection."
mina: Also add a tiny benchmark row comparing q4_0 vs fp16 at batch sizes 1 and 16, with footnote "results vary by GPU family and exec kernel". Don't embed huge tables.
ralph: Good. i'll leave a TODO to update the generated HTML table from the CSV (automation follow-up). We should not hard-code the table in the card.
sasha: Snippet draft for review:
```js
// SDK v4: prefer quantized, fallback to compat alias
const v = await client.models.resolveVariant('polaris13b', { preferQuantized: true });
try {
  const r = await client.generate({ model: v, input: prompt });
  console.log(r.generated_text);
} catch (e) {
  const fallback = 'polaris13b-compat-q4_0';
  const r2 = await client.generate({ model: fallback, input: prompt });
  console.log(r2.generated_text);
}
```
mina: looks good. add one-line CLI example too: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -d '{"model":"polaris13b:compat-q4_0","input":"..."}'`
ralph: will add that. Also remember to remove stray trailing commas in JSON examples (jen caught that last time).
docs-bot: Deploy preview: https://deploy-preview.redwood-docs.io/pr-4782 (CI #11890) :white_check_mark:
cheng: small editorial: add an explicit compat note: "If a requested variant is unavailable, the runtime will select the closest compatible alias (e.g., compat-q4_0)." That helps reduce confusing 404s in logs.
ralph: done. merging plan: small copy edits today, wait 48h for runtime to confirm ceilings, then merge and open CSV sync PR. i'll ping here if anything blocks. thanks all!
